From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 20:43:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] Build the SEI crosswalk: schema, connector, API and
 dashboard
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds the IMDS/STAR/UAF/SEI crosswalk to Lineage 360 without touching PBDW.

PBDW IS UNCHANGED, and that is a property of the data rather than a flag.
No existing table is altered, no existing loader is edited, no existing
endpoint changes its query. CrosswalkDashboard renders an empty state for a
warehouse with no crosswalk rows, so PBDW keeps today's screens until its own
workbook is ingested.

sql/51_sei_crosswalk.sql creates nine tables and seeds three lanes. The
contract field's type goes in legacy_src_column, a side table keyed the way
legacy_source_file is, rather than as three new columns on legacy_lineage —
so no ALTER lands on a table PBDW depends on. The lane needs no new column
either: legacy_source_file already carries source_system, so lane resolves as
(source_system, data_source).

ingestion/lane_lineage_conn.py is a new connector, not an edit to
legacy_lineage_conn.py, for the reason legacy_source_file_conn.py records:
the repo copy of that file is older than the copy running, and editing a
stale file has broken working screens before. It folds header case, spaces
and underscores, which fixes the failure that would otherwise have been
silent — LINEAGE_MAP looks up DWH_Target_Table by exact key while the
workbook emits DWH_TARGET_TABLE, so every row would be skipped for want of a
target and the load would report zero rows with no error. It also accepts
SUBJECT_AREA into functional_group so _legacy_groups.py's resolver chain has
something to resolve, and ships CP_SEI_RELOAD for a scoped purge rather than
leaving upsert-never-delete to be cleaned up later the way sql/49 had to be.

routers_sei_crosswalk.py adds eight read-only endpoints. Link weights count
DISTINCT target columns, never rows, because legacy_lineage's grain is
(target column x source) and counting rows double-counts a fan-in.

CrosswalkDashboard fills the slot LineageHome already reserved: scope === "sei"
rendered a placeholder panel for the SWP programme. Drill-down is a stack, so
Back returns to where the click came from. The six divergence shapes are drawn
rather than described — collapse fans out, dual source converges, bypass arcs
over a hollow node.

Verified: both new UI files and LineageHome parse under the project's own
esbuild. `npm run build` fails on DocDrill.jsx importing mermaid, which is
absent from package.json — confirmed pre-existing by building with these
changes stashed and getting the identical error. Not introduced here, and
documented in INSTALL rather than silently worked around.

