From d436a992485057b83de9eff118d0f0cd0a5bcd7d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 20:54:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] Fix a destructive purge, and support attaching a
 crosswalk to an existing baseline
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Answering "how do we ingest the PBDW mapping" exposed a bug in the connector
shipped in c5cc8b2: _purge deleted legacy_lineage WHERE data_source = :ds
unconditionally. Run with CP_SEI_DATA_SOURCE=PBDW and CP_SEI_RELOAD=1 and it
would have deleted all 1,180 PBDW lineage rows that legacy_lineage_conn.py
loaded from the AddVantage workbook. The IMDS case hid it: IMDS had no
baseline, so there was nothing to destroy.

PBDW is the opposite case. Its baseline already exists, so the crosswalk
workbook supplies only the SEI side. The connector now has a lineage mode:

  load    this workbook supplies the baseline   (IMDS)
  attach  a baseline exists, SEI side only      (PBDW)
  auto    count existing rows and decide

In attach mode it writes neither legacy_lineage nor legacy_source_file, and
purges neither even with CP_SEI_RELOAD=1. auto is the default but INSTALL
tells you to set attach explicitly for PBDW, because the cost of being wrong
is asymmetric and an explicit value cannot be surprised by an empty database.

The join differs too. IMDS contract fields are STAR field names and match
literally; PBDW contract fields are AddVantage codes, and the same field is
BI/2-1 on one sheet and BI_2_L1 on another. Both sides are now stored and
joined canonically: _norm_code in the loader, a matching SQL canon in the
router, and src_col_norm columns added by sql/52. Unit-checked both ways,
including that the _L(\d+) backreference survives as a raw string — in a
plain string Python turns it into chr(1) and the collapse silently stops,
which is the same trap _legacy_groups.py documents.

Attach mode ends by reporting how many SEI mappings fail to resolve to an
existing lineage row. On PBDW that number matters more than the row count:
non-zero means either net-new scope or a field code the canon cannot
reconcile, and the two are indistinguishable in a spreadsheet.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FxshfJgezPNjLcAKY1MsJW
