docs/sei-crosswalk/COPY-AND-INSTALL.md separates the seven new files, which
copy whole, from the three existing files, which must NOT be copied whole.
Enterprise copies of LineageHome.jsx, run.py and main.py are likely ahead of
this branch, and overwriting them reverts work — the failure
legacy_source_file_conn.py already records for api.js, mockData.js and
routers_legacy_lineage.py. All three edits are reproduced in full so they can
be applied by hand, with a fallback statement of what the LineageHome edit has
to achieve if the surrounding code has diverged.

docs/ingestion-prompts/PROMPT_PBDW_ADDVANTAGE_SEI_crosswalk.md is the attach
case. It carries no lineage sheet: PBDW's baseline exists and is not the
workbook's to restate.

Its load-bearing rule is that TARGET_CONTRACT_FIELD may only hold a value
copied verbatim from a contract inventory extracted from legacy_lineage. An
AddVantage field code is BI/1-1 in one place and BI_2_L1 in another; the
ingester reconciles those two spellings but cannot reconcile an invented
value, a business name or a DWH column name. Supplying the inventory as an
input is what makes a zero unmatched count reachable, and the prompt asks for
that count first in the reply. VERIFY is likewise pinned to a target inventory
extract rather than to whatever the model believes PBDW contains.

