The previous revision framed CP_SEI_LINEAGE_MODE=load as a fallback and the
legacy_dictionary route as preferred. That was wrong and it muddied a design
that was already settled.

The crosswalk workbook IS the IMDS lineage document. LANE_LINEAGE is one row
per (lane, target table, target column) with the full DWH/STG2/STG1/SRC chain,
mirroring LEGACY_LINEAGE one for one, and VERIFY is pinned to the same row
set. STAR -> IMDS was never in legacy_lineage — that absence is the finding
this work started from — so there is no baseline to attach to and nothing to
conflict with. load is the normal path for IMDS and the one the mockups were
built on.

CP_LEGACY_SOURCES remains worth knowing about, but only if an authoritative
IMDS mapping workbook turns up, at which point the crosswalk switches to
attach and IMDS matches PBDW's arrangement.

Two things from the previous revision survive because they are true
independent of the framing: load the baseline once from one source, with the
detection query for a duplicated baseline; and the current workbook covers
three of seven STAR feed families, which is an input gap to close by attaching
the other four lineage documents and re-running the prompt, not a reason to
change route.

