+  <h1>Observation model</h1>
+  <p class="lede">All intraday and EOD data now arrives as SDC events and moves through one pipeline to Stage&nbsp;1, Stage&nbsp;2 and Gold. Monitoring it needs two clocks, not one.</p>
+
+  <div class="note">
+    <span class="note-h">Two clocks</span>
+    <p><strong>Intraday is continuous.</strong> There is no "complete" — only flowing at an acceptable rate, or falling behind. Health is lag, boxing continuity and Stage 1 load success over a rolling window.</p>
+    <p><strong>EOD is a gate.</strong> Completeness is binary: EOD marker received, every micro-batch for the date <code>LOADED</code>, transformation run, reconciliation clean, <code>DATE_CONTROL</code> at <code>COMPLETE</code>.</p>
+    <p>On one clock the screen is either permanently amber, because intraday is never finished, or blind to an EOD running two hours late.</p>
+  </div>
