+  <h1>API surface and the error taxonomy</h1>
+  <p class="lede">Twenty-two operations. Twenty-one are reads; the twenty-second is the endpoint SEI calls. The full contract is <code>integration360-openapi.yaml</code>.</p>
+
+  <h2>Error taxonomy — three classes, three owners</h2>
+  <p>The axis that decides who is woken up, and whether a retry is legitimate at all. Without it the exception list is one undifferentiated pile that nobody owns.</p>
+  <div class="tscroll"><table>
+    <thead><tr><th style="width:13%">Class</th><th style="width:19%">Owner</th><th>What it means</th><th style="width:26%">Retry</th></tr></thead>
+    <tbody>
+      <tr><td><span class="pill p-warn">BUSINESS</span></td><td>Operations and the source</td><td>The data is wrong — a missing mandatory attribute, a code outside its domain, an unresolved reference, a control total that does not tie.</td><td><strong>Never.</strong> Retrying produces the same rejection and spends the attempt budget.</td></tr>
+      <tr><td><span class="pill p-ext">TECHNICAL</span></td><td>Engineering</td><td>The pipeline is wrong — a transformation failed, a model test failed, a schema mismatch, an unparseable envelope.</td><td>Only after a fix. An unchanged retry is an unchanged failure.</td></tr>
+      <tr><td><span class="pill p-ok">SYSTEM</span></td><td>Platform</td><td>The platform is wrong — a timeout, a lost connection, a pod eviction, a broker rebalance, a rate limit.</td><td>The only class where blind retry is legitimate, and the only one with a circuit breaker behind it.</td></tr>
+    </tbody>
+  </table></div>
+  <div class="note">
+    <span class="note-h">Why the class matters more than the count</span>
+    <p>A day that is ninety percent SYSTEM is a platform incident. A day that is ninety percent BUSINESS is a source data problem. The same total means opposite things. <code>/errors/summary</code> exists to make that shape visible in one call, and <code>top_codes[].delta_vs_baseline_pct</code> is there because a code that normally fires twice and fired two hundred times is the signal — the absolute count is not.</p>
